Where the version is kept from one launch to the next; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/FileVersionStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore.defaultDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"notificationCenter","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the platform posts its lifecycle notifications; the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"center by default."}]}]},{"name":"file","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller’s file; leave it to its default."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"fileID","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The caller’s module and file name; leave it to its default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"function","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller’s enclosing declaration; leave it to its default."}]}]},{"name":"line","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The caller’s line; leave it to its default.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"column","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The caller’s column; leave it to its default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The observation, which tracks until it is cancelled, finished or released.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is tracked until this is called. Call it as the app launches, such as in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"application delegate’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and keep what it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["lifecycle = tracker.trackLifecycle()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As it starts, it compares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" with the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"versionStore"},{"type":"text","text":" saved: none tracks an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"install, another an update, the same neither; it then saves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":". Then it tracks an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"open, not from the background. After that, each transition tracks once, however many times"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is reported:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS, iPadOS, tvOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst: "},{"code":"UIApplication","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s notifications. Entering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the background tracks "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationBackgrounded"},{"type":"text","text":", returning to the foreground"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationOpened"},{"type":"text","text":" from the background, and terminating "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationTerminated"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A scene-based app gets them once for the whole app, not per scene."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"watchOS: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKApplication"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s, without termination, which watchOS doesn’t report."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"macOS: ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSApplication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s. Another app becoming active counts as the background, this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one becoming active again as the foreground.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Linux: no notifications; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/LifecycleObservation\/finish()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" tracks the termination.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Leaving the foreground, it also makes the tracker’s records durable: it waits for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s worker to write every record tracked so far to the tracker’s store, then calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"synchronize()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A delivery batched with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/LifecycleBatchStrategy","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is pending as it reads the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationBackgrounded","type":"reference"},{"text":" record. A notification’s handler only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands the transition on; the tracking, the version store and the store’s work run on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"task of their own, never on the thread that posted it. Where the system suspends an app in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background (all but macOS and Mac Catalyst), the handler asks it for background time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), held until the records are durable. A termination’s records are made durable the same way, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holding the main thread up: what the process doesn’t finish before it exits is what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s documented loss window takes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps no state outside what it returns. Two calls observe twice, so call it once per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/lifecycletracking\/trackers\/tracker\/tracklifecycle(kinds:version:versionstore:notificationcenter:file:fileid:function:line:column:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/Trackers\/Tracker\/trackLifecycle(kinds:version:versionStore:notificationCenter:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/Trackers","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/Trackers\/Tracker"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/LifecycleTracking\/Tracker+TrackLifecycle.swift#L63","fileName":"Tracker+TrackLifecycle.swift"},"title":"trackLifecycle(kinds:version:versionStore:notificationCenter:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trackLifecycle","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"t